## Control {{controlId}}: Implement Cryptographic Mechanisms to Protect CUI on Digital Media During Transport

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization implements cryptographic protections for CUI on digital media during transport within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through BitLocker encryption, sensitivity label encryption, and TLS enforcement managed by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

{{#if bitLockerEnforced}}
**Endpoint Media Encryption:**
BitLocker Drive Encryption protects CUI on {{deviceCount}} managed devices during physical transport. Full-disk encryption ensures data remains protected if devices are lost or intercepted during transit.
{{/if}}

{{#if compliancePolicyActive}}
**Compliance-Enforced Encryption:**
Intune compliance policy "{{policyName}}" requires encryption on all devices, ensuring CUI is cryptographically protected before any transport scenario.
{{/if}}

**Transport Encryption Standards:**
- **Email:** Sensitivity label encryption (AES-256) protects CUI email attachments during transport; TLS 1.2+ for SMTP transport
- **File Sharing:** SharePoint/OneDrive use HTTPS (TLS 1.2+) for all file transfers; sensitivity labels maintain encryption at rest and in transit
- **Removable Media:** USB drives containing CUI must be encrypted with BitLocker To Go or equivalent FIPS 140-2 validated encryption before transport
- **Physical Transport:** Devices in transit maintain BitLocker encryption; recovery keys stored securely in Entra ID

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine BitLocker deployment reports, sensitivity label encryption settings, TLS configuration, and removable media encryption policy.

